### Test Organization
1. File Structure:
   - Tests mirror source structure in `__tests__` directory
   - Co-locate test helpers with relevant tests
   - Keep setup files at root of test directory
   - Group related test utilities

2. Naming Conventions:
   - Test files: `ComponentName.test.tsx`
   - Test utilities: `ComponentName.test.utils.ts`
   - Mock files: `__mocks__/moduleName.ts`
   - Setup files: `setup.js` or `setupTests.js`

3. Progressive Testing Strategy:
   - Start with minimal test infrastructure
   - Focus on core functionality first
   - Add complexity only when needed
   - Avoid premature optimization
   - Keep mocks simple and focused
   - Expand coverage gradually

4. Mocking Guidelines:
   Priority Order:
   1. Core functionality only
   2. Essential React Native components
   3. Basic animation support
   4. Required platform features
   
   Avoid Early:
   - Complex animation mocks
   - Full platform feature sets
   - Edge case handling
   - Comprehensive error simulation

### React Native Testing Setup
// Implementation of:
// - @project-structure.mdc#Testing-Strategy#Test-Setup
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Error-Handling#Testing

1. Initial Setup - Keep Minimal:
   ```javascript
   module.exports = {
     preset: 'react-native',
     setupFiles: ['<rootDir>/src/__tests__/setup.js'],
     testEnvironment: 'jsdom',
     moduleNameMapper: {
       '^@/(.*)$': '<rootDir>/src/$1'
     }
   };
   ```

2. Essential Mocks Only:
   ```javascript
   // Basic React Native component mocks
   const mockComponent = (name) => {
     return function(props) {
       return React.createElement('view', { ...props, testID: name });
     };
   };

   // Core component mocks
   jest.mock('react-native', () => ({
     View: mockComponent('View'),
     Text: mockComponent('Text'),
     TouchableOpacity: mockComponent('TouchableOpacity'),
     Animated: {
       View: mockComponent('AnimatedView'),
       Value: function(value) {
         this.value = value;
         this.setValue = jest.fn();
       },
       timing: () => ({ start: jest.fn() })
     }
   }));
   ```

3. Expand Only When Needed:
   - Add mocks as required by tests
   - Document why each mock is needed
   - Remove unused mocks
   - Keep setup file clean and focused

### Component Testing Standards
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Quality-Gates#Testing
// - @battle-animation-standards.mdc#Technical-Requirements#Testing

1. Required Test Cases:
   - Basic rendering
   - Props validation
   - User interactions
   - State changes
   - Error boundaries
   - Animation triggers
   - Style applications

2. Animation Testing:
   - Mock Animated.Value for synchronous tests
   - Verify animation triggers
   - Test style interpolations
   - Check transform applications
   - Validate cleanup

3. Style Testing:
   - Verify base styles
   - Test conditional styles
   - Check dynamic calculations
   - Validate theme compliance
   - Test responsive behavior

### Performance Testing
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Core-Requirements#Testing
